/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/Male-formation.dat -- the first 2 dissociations of maleic acid, written from the neutral master:
      H2Male  <=>  Male + 2 H+

  logK25 and dH are the selected values of Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231, Table 7.42 (Maleate), p. 305 (evaluation grades CBD / BBD,
  scale: standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K, I = 0):
      pK1 = 1.92, pK2 = 6.27
      dH1 = 1.1 kJ/mol, dH2 = -3.6 kJ/mol
  This record carries the sum of those steps (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The enthalpy is the EVALUATED dH_ion of the same table as the pK, not a difference of formation
  enthalpies: the two kinds of number are kept apart and cross-checked in
  docs/design/organic-acids-in-the-catalogue.md.  Hand-curated organic chemistry, not PHREEQC.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species Male; masters ( { ion H2Male; nu 1; } { ion H; nu -2; } );
      logK25 -8.19; dH -2500; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231, Table 7.42 (Maleate), p. 305: pK1 = 1.92, pK2 = 6.27; dH1 = 1.1 kJ/mol, dH2 = -3.6 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K, I = 0)";
